        "original_id": "4a96852a-eb50-5ad1-b118-b1a4331b8702",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Rob Bottin, David Fincher, John Carpenter, Paul Verhoeven\n- Roles: special make-up effects creator, director, producer\n- Works: The Fog, The Thing, RoboCop, Total Recall, Basic Instinct, Se7en, Fight Club, The Curious Case of Benjamin Button, The Social Network\n- Awards: Academy Award for Best Director, Golden Globe Award for Best Director, BAFTA Award for Best Direction\n\nFacts:\n- Rob Bottin, born Robin R. Bottin on April 1, 1959, is an American special make-up effects creator.\n- David Fincher, born David Andrew Leo Fincher on August 28, 1962, is an American director and producer known for films, television series, and music videos.\n- Rob Bottin collaborated with director John Carpenter on The Fog and The Thing.\n- Rob Bottin collaborated with director Paul Verhoeven on RoboCop, Total Recall, and Basic Instinct.\n- Rob Bottin collaborated with director David Fincher on Se7en and Fight Club.\n- David Fincher was nominated for the Academy Award for Best Director for The Curious Case of Benjamin Button (2008).\n- David Fincher was nominated for the Academy Award for Best Director for The Social Network (2010).\n- David Fincher won the Golden Globe Award for Best Director and the BAFTA Award for Best Direction for The Social Network.",
